  "slug": "apple-brine-for-turkey-the-night-before-cooking",
  "name": "Apple Brine for Turkey the Night Before Cooking",
  "recipe_type": "drink",
  "brief_description": "Try this apple brine recipe with apple juice, salt, garlic, water, and ice for turkey the night before cooking to help get a moist, fall-apart turkey.",
  "cuisine": "American",
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "Line a cooler with a large food-safe bag. Add 1 gallon water, apple juice, and salt to the bag; stir until salt is dissolved. Add garlic."
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "text": "To use, place turkey in brine, breast-side down; add more water as needed until turkey is completely submerged. Pour ice over turkey. Seal the bag, close the cooler, and let turkey brine overnight."
    }
  ],
